From 8402dfec338a628893fc0913751eee5031660113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olympia <olympia@xbmc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:30:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Update only the changed movie after the information
 dialog

[GUI] Allow GUI_MSG_REFRESH_THUMBS to be limited to one item (837cad7)

A thumbs refresh made every media window free the layouts of all its
list items, so changing the art of one video loaded every poster of the
list again. The message can now carry the changed item, and a media
window then frees only the list items matching it. Other windows and
controls handle the message as before.

The video information dialog and the video art chooser send the changed
item along.

[Video] Update only the changed movie after the information dialog (9f78472)

Changing the art of a movie or refreshing it from the information dialog
reloaded the whole list, and every poster of it was loaded again. For a
movie the window now updates the one list item in place: the refreshed
movie is queried again the way the listing did, as the refresh adds it
with a new id, and its art is reloaded. The list is only sorted again
and rebound when the order changed. The disc cache of the list is still
removed.

Everything else, or a refresh which may change what a filter or the
movie set grouping shows, still refreshes the whole list. This now also
happens when a failed refresh removed the movie from the library, which
left it in the list before.

[Video] Update only the changed movie after Manage > Choose art (2ab8074)

Choosing art for a movie through the Manage context menu still reloaded
the whole list. The art is set on the list item itself, so the window
now only reloads the art of that item, the same way as after the
information dialog. Other Manage actions and other media types still
refresh the whole list.

Backported to Kodi 21.3-Omega (a3a448d) for the OSMC vero5 build from
xbmc/xbmc#30164 (2ab8074), its three commits squashed, so
UpdateMovieListItem() is declared protected right away.

Omega's CGUIWindowVideoBase::ShowInfo() returns a bool and has no
ShowInfoResult, and the enum's using declaration needs C++20. ShowInfo()
keeps its bool and reports the in place update through two new out
parameters instead: updatedItem is set where upstream returns
RESULT_OK_ART_UPDATED or RESULT_OK_INFO_REFRESHED, and infoRefreshed
tells the two apart. ShowInfoAndRefresh() still calls Refresh() without
clearing the cache, as Omega did.

Omega has no CGUIMediaWindow::RemoveDiscCache(directory), so the list's
own disc cache is removed with m_vecItems->RemoveDiscCache(GetID()), as
Omega's Refresh(true) does. Other Omega names: m_type and MediaTypeMovie
for GetMediaType() and MEDIA::TYPE::MOVIE, m_set.id for m_set.GetID(),
CFileItemList::IsVideoDb() for VIDEO::IsVideoDb(),
NODE_TYPE_TITLE_MOVIES for NodeType::TITLE_MOVIES, the member
CFileItem::FillInDefaultIcon() for ART::FillInDefaultIcon(), and the
"thumb" and "ParentPath" strings for the ART and ITEM constants.
std::ranges::equal is replaced by std::equal for C++17.

Three changes differ from upstream. Omega patches a movie with versions
into the folder of its versions after loading, when the
videolibrary.showvideoversionsasfolder setting is on, and the item
queried again lacks that, so such a list item is left to a full refresh.
The thumb loader is stopped before the list item is read, not only
before it is changed, as the loader thread writes it. In the files view
the copy of the list item gets its database id cleared before its
details are loaded again, so a copy the library has no match for is no
longer taken for the refreshed movie when the refresh reused the id.
